# The vendored files are byte-exact copies of upstream, verified by SHA-256 in
# _vendor/VENDORED.json. Those hashes are computed over the LF-normalized bytes
# git stores. On a checkout with core.autocrlf=true the working tree gets CRLF,
# so `refresh.sh --check` hashes different bytes and reports DRIFT on files that
# are pristine — disabling the one integrity control the vendoring rule has.
#
# Pin the vendored tree to LF so the working tree always matches the manifest.
src/wm_hook/_vendor/** text eol=lf

# The hook's own sources and the corpora it is tested against must not be
# rewritten by git either: line endings are part of what this tool preserves,
# and a CRLF-mangled fixture silently invalidates the fidelity tests.
src/wm_hook/*.py text eol=lf
tests/corpus/** -text
*.sh text eol=lf
